  "head": {
   "ref": "fix/plugin-locations-workspace-scope",
   "sha": "a52e5906c4d0d4f605e93942e3224235bc7f8c35",
   "repo": "nalmiron/vscode",
   "label": "nalmiron:fix/plugin-locations-workspace-scope"
  },
  "base": {
   "ref": "main",
   "sha": "ce386f1a861ac8ec0e54afa5d5b5bc9adcbca3db"
  },
  "body": "Changes the scope of `chat.pluginLocations` from `ConfigurationScope.MACHINE` to `ConfigurationScope.WINDOW`, allowing it to be set in workspace settings (`.vscode/settings.json`).\n\n`restricted: true` is preserved — workspace trust still gates the setting.\n\n## Motivation\n\n`chat.pluginLocations` is the only customization location setting restricted to user settings. The comparable settings are all workspace-scoped:\n\n| Setting | Scope |\n|---|---|\n| `chat.hookFilesLocations` | `WINDOW` |\n| `chat.agentSkillsLocations` | `WINDOW` |\n| `chat.agentFilesLocations` | `WINDOW` |\n| `chat.instructionsFilesLocations` | `WINDOW` |\n| **`chat.pluginLocations`** | **`MACHINE`** |\n\nA plugin bundles components (skills, agents, hooks, MCP servers) that are individually workspace-configurable. The bundle's scope should be consistent.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Build: 0 errors\n- Unit tests: 22,511 passing (1 pre-existing Kerberos failure, also fails on main)\n- Functional: workspace-relative path in `.vscode/settings.json` accepted, plugin discovered and skill visible in chat\n\n## Use case\n\nTeams maintaining workspace frameworks need to configure plugin directories in `.vscode/settings.json` so teammates get the same plugins on clone. Today this requires each developer to manually add entries to user settings, which doesn't scale.\n\nThe path resolution code (`_resolvePluginPath`) already handles workspace-relative paths — this change only unblocks the setting from being written to workspace settings.\n\nFixes #303853\nRelated: #307040, #308791",
  "rebaseable": true
 },
